  "plan": {
    "goal": "Establish a lung alveolar-capillary barrier chip under perfusion at very low physiological shear (0.03 Pa / 0.3 dyn/cm²) to model alveolar epithelial-endothelial interface conditions.",
    "rationale": "Target wall shear stress of 0.03 Pa falls within the physiological alveolar shear range for A549 (0.02–0.05 Pa per the physiology registry). A wide, shallow channel (1000 µm × 100 µm) mimics the thin, broad alveolar-capillary interface. At 3.0 µL/min this geometry yields 0.03 Pa shear, laminar flow (Re ≈ 0.09), negligible pressure drop (12 Pa), and a 40 s residence time. A549 seeded at 10000 cells/cm² over a 0.2 cm² membrane gives 2000 cells, with perfused O2 supply ~166× demand (no hypoxia). HUVEC can be co-cultured on the opposing (basal) side for a full barrier, though its physiological shear range (0.1–1.0 Pa) is higher than the alveolar target — the 0.03 Pa target is chosen to protect the alveolar epithelium, the shear-sensitive readout here.",
