    "caveats": [
      "Verify the actual channel cross-section (width × height) with profilometry — shear scales as 1/h², so a 10% height error shifts shear ~20%.",
      "Confirm medium viscosity (assumed 1e-3 Pa·s); serum-containing medium is slightly higher (~1.1e-3), which would raise shear ~10% at the same flow.",
      "A549 barrier function is modest; if a tight alveolar barrier (TEER) is the readout, consider a primary alveolar epithelial line or co-culture with HUVEC on the basal side.",
      "If HUVEC is co-cultured, note its physiological shear range (0.1–1.0 Pa) exceeds the 0.03 Pa alveolar target — endothelial health should be confirmed by morphology/junctional markers rather than shear conditioning.",
      "Use a syringe pump capable of stable low flow (3 µL/min); check for pulsation that could transiently exceed the shear target.",
      "Confirm the membrane growth area (assumed 0.2 cm²) matches the actual insert/chip footprint before seeding."
    ]
